---
import CompareLayout from '../../layouts/CompareLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/urls';

const appStoreUrl = 'https://apps.shopify.com/blocklist';
---

<CompareLayout
	title="Blox vs Blockify: blocklist-first vs fraud scoring"
	description="Compare Blox and Blockify for Shopify fraud prevention: community customer blocklist and identity linking vs IP, bot, and country-style fraud filtering."
>
	<span class="section-label">Comparison</span>
	<h1>Blox vs Blockify: blocklist-first vs fraud scoring</h1>
	<p class="section-lead">
		Merchants searching for Shopify <strong>fraud prevention</strong> often compare a <em>customer blocklist</em> to a <em>fraud filter</em>. Here’s a clear head-to-head. For NoFraud and Signifyd as well, see <a href={withBase('compare/')}>Blox vs NoFraud, Signifyd, and Blockify</a>.
	</p>

	<section class="compare__block" aria-labelledby="positioning">
		<h2 id="positioning">The short version</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Blox</strong> is blocklist-first: every identifier a customer uses is grouped
			into one profile automatically, so blocking fraudsters, chargeback abusers, serial
			returners, and refund abusers takes one action, and that decision is shared across a
			merchant network.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Blockify</strong> is commonly used as a fraud-filtering / blocking toolkit
			oriented around signals like IP, bots, and country-style controls (plus a large App
			Store footprint). It’s closer to “score and filter the session” than “remember this
			customer forever across stores.”
		</p>
		<p>
			Blox is built for <strong>repeat chargebacks</strong> and multi-account abuse. Blockify is a filter-first app for bots and geo/IP noise.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="compare__block" aria-labelledby="table-heading">
		<h2 id="table-heading">Side-by-side</h2>
		<div class="compare__table-wrap">
			<table>
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th>Dimension</th>
						<th>Blox</th>
						<th>Blockify (typical use)</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Primary model</th>
						<td>Community customer blocklist with automatic identity linking</td>
						<td>Fraud filtering / blockers (IP, bot, country, etc.)</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Best against</th>
						<td>Chargebacks, serial returners, refund abuse, duplicate accounts</td>
						<td>Bots, unwanted geos, session-level abuse patterns</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Decision style</th>
						<td>Explicit block; simple rules; network flags for review</td>
						<td>Filter / score / block traffic patterns</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Cross-store memory</th>
						<td>Yes: when one store flags fraud, others can be protected</td>
						<td>Not the core product story</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Shopify focus</th>
						<td>
							<a href={appStoreUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">Blox on the App Store</a>
						</td>
						<td>Large installed base; filter-oriented positioning</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>

	<p class="compare__cta">
		<a class="btn" href={appStoreUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">Install Blox on Shopify</a>
	</p>
	<p class="compare__more">
		<a href={withBase('compare/')}>Blox vs NoFraud, Signifyd, and Blockify</a>
		<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
		<a href={withBase('faq/')}>FAQ</a>
		<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
		<a href={withBase('guides/how-to-block-repeat-chargeback-customers/')}>How to block repeat chargeback customers</a>
		<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
		<a href={withBase('guides/blocklist-vs-fraud-filter/')}>Blocklist vs fraud filter</a>
	</p>
</CompareLayout>
